# trip-polama Design System

Product-facing UI must not show environment-variable names, server paths, ports,
API routes, startup commands or developer configuration forms. Keep those in
README/admin documentation. Explain assistant capabilities, limits and privacy
in everyday language; preserve meaningful user approval controls.

Photo UX: never ask for filenames. Use an image file picker for uploads and a
separate getUserMedia camera preview with a capture button. Do not use a file
input with capture as the camera experience; browsers may ignore that hint.
Stop all camera tracks on capture, close or unmount. Preview before saving.
Store image blobs locally for offline use; explain any future network upload.

trip-polama uses a **light theme only**, with a natural palette that blends with the
outdoors: **sky blue + green**. Do not introduce dark mode, new color ramps, or
one-off hex values. Always use the CSS tokens below; extend `--token` values, never
hard-code colors in components.

<rule>
name: trip_polama_design_system
description: Enforce the light nature theme and palette tokens in all UI code
filters:
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)(color|theme|palette|style|design|css|styling|dark|light)"
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.(css|tsx|ts|html|svg)$"

actions:
  - type: enforce
    message: |
      TRIP-POLAMA DESIGN RULES

      THEME
      - Light theme only. No dark mode. `color-scheme: light`.
      - Feels natural/outdoorsy: sky blue + green, airy whites.

      PALETTE (CSS custom properties in apps/web/src/styles.css)
      - --bg:        #f2f7fb   (soft sky wash)
      - --panel:     #ffffff   (surfaces)
      - --panel-2:   #eaf3f9   (sky tint, inputs/lists)
      - --border:    #cfe3f0   (sky borders)
      - --text:      #14303f   (deep forest/sky)
      - --muted:     #5c7484   (secondary text)
      - --accent:    #16a34a   (nature green — primary actions)
      - --accent-2:  #22c55e   (green hover)
      - --sky:       #2b8bc2   (sky blue — secondary actions, links)
      - --sky-2:     #6cb5dd   (sky hover)
      - --warn:      #d97706
      - --danger:    #dc2626
      - --radius:    12px

      USAGE
      - Primary buttons: green (--accent), white text.
      - Secondary buttons / links: sky blue (--sky), white text.
      - Active tab underline: green (--accent).
      - Offline/local "brain" indicators: green = on, muted = off.
      - Surfaces: white panels on the sky-wash background with sky borders.

      RULES
      - Reference tokens (var(--accent)), never literal hex in components.
      - If a new color is genuinely needed, add it as a token here first, then use it.
      - Update this file and apps/web/src/styles.css together.

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
  enforcement: strict
</rule>
